"""English quick guide; shortcuts transcribed from the official V2 manual."""
SECTIONS=[
('Getting started', 'Connect the TH80 Pro V2 over USB with the mode switch in the middle. Close other configurators, run Open.cmd from Explorer and click Connect keyboard. This app is still in development; see below for what has been confirmed so far.'),
('Photo and GIF', 'In the Screen & GIF tab, choose a file and check the preview. The screen is 240 × 135 pixels. The app crops images to the center and fits GIFs to at most 18 frames per slot. Sending replaces both saved images, and the previous images are not backed up. Keep the cable connected until it finishes.'),
('Clock', 'Set time and show clock sends this computer\'s date and time. Back to saved image does not delete any images. The clock shown in the app is a preview of the computer\'s clock.'),
('Keys and undo', 'Click Read keys and lighting, choose the layer and click a key. Pick the function and apply it. The app checks the previous value, saves a copy and reads the result back after writing. Undo last change restores the last key. Reading, writing and restoring were confirmed in this keyboard\'s logs.'),
('Lighting: keyboard shortcuts', 'From the official TH80 Pro V2 manual:\n\nFn + Backspace: lighting on/off\nFn + \\: cycle RGB effects\nFn + ↑ / ↓: brightness up/down\nFn + → / ←: hue up/down\nFn + = / -: speed up/down\nFn + [ / ]: adjust saturation\n\nIn the Lighting tab, click Check lighting. The app reads brightness through the native protocol when VIA does not expose it. Use levels 0 to 9 (the range observed on this keyboard) and apply. Changing brightness from the app was confirmed by the user and by the keyboard\'s final read. The app offers the observed effects 1, 3, 13 and 16 and speed levels 2 and 4. Choose Keep current to leave a setting as it is. Effect and speed were confirmed on the keyboard by the user and in the logs. The Color option offers Yellow-green, Green and Rainbow, reproducing states captured on this keyboard. All three were confirmed by the user on the physical keyboard and in the logs. The list now also imports other states seen in captures. See HEX color and catalog below.'),
('HEX color and catalog', 'Click Color wheel / HEX, pick on the wheel or type #0066FF, click Use color and then Apply lighting. The color depends on the active effect. Choosing a color does not send anything by itself. Arbitrary RGB still needs visual confirmation on the TH80.\n\nTo grow the effect and speed lists, change the setting with the physical shortcut and click Add current state. That button only reads the keyboard and saves the state to the local catalog. Earlier captures are imported when the app opens. Choose Keep current to leave effect, speed or color unchanged.'),
('Lighting diagnostics', '1. In the Lighting tab, click 1 · Capture before.\n2. Press Fn + ↓ once or twice and check that the brightness dropped. Change only the brightness. If it is already at minimum, use Fn + ↑.\n3. Wait two seconds and click 2 · Capture after.\n4. Ask the assistant to analyze the logs.\n\nCapturing only reads settings; it does not change the configuration. Differences in the data still need interpreting and do not, on their own, prove lighting support.'),
('Screen and connection', 'Fn + Enter: switch screen content\nFn + X: screen on/off\nFn + A: Windows mode\nFn + S: Mac mode\n\nUSB: switch in the middle with the cable connected. Bluetooth: switch to the left. 2.4 GHz: switch to the right. This version of TH80 Studio uses USB only.'),
('Logs and current status', 'Still photo confirmed visually. GIF and clock are confirmed in the logs. Keys: reading, changing and restoring confirmed by the keyboard. Lighting: brightness, available effects, available speed levels and three color options confirmed on the keyboard.\n\nResults are written to result-*.json files. The logs-via and logs-lighting folders keep attempts for diagnostics. The app does not change firmware, drivers or Windows protections.'),
('Official manual', 'The button above opens EPOMAKER\'s official page to read or download the manual. Source: https://epomaker.com/blogs/manuals/th80-pro-v2-manual\n\nThe shortcuts listed are the manufacturer\'s defaults; remapping keys can change how they behave.')
]
